  "user_impact": "Users with attention or cognitive impairments, and screen reader users, are distracted or disrupted by continuously running motion they cannot turn off.",
  "technical_impact": "`<marquee>` element without pause control, or an element with animation-iteration-count: infinite exceeding 5 seconds per cycle with no detectable pause control or prefers-reduced-motion support.",
  "source": "WCAG 2.2 SC 2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide (moving content that lasts more than five seconds)",
  "applicability": "Rendered elements with a running animation whose iteration count is infinite, and marquee elements.",
  "expectation": "A review at the outermost endlessly animated element (one per group of\nsiblings) when the page offers no control to pause or stop motion. A finite\nanimation (iteration count 3) is not endless; an endless animation on an\nelement that is not rendered moves nothing. A control labelled to pause or\nstop (button \"Pause animation\") is taken as the mechanism; whether it works\nis for a human. An animation started by a script after load counts like a\nstatic one. Review, not a violation: an animation may end within five\nseconds of the page's own logic, which the snapshot cannot see.",
  "method": "shared",
